<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Minor C. Keith</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1848–1929</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Minor Cooper Keith</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Minor Cooper Keith was an American businessman who built the railway from Costa Rica's Central Valley to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> coast between 1871 and 1890. He planted bananas along the line to provide freight, and in 1899 his banana business merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-fruit-company">United Fruit Company</a>. He went on to control railways and plantations across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/minor-c-keith.jpg" alt="Minor C. Keith" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Minor_Cooper_Keith_in_1917.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
